arePseudoInverses -- check the Penrose relations for the pseudo inverse
***********************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        arePseudoInverses(A,B)
        arePseudoInverses(C,Cplus)
  * Inputs:
      * A, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, 
      * B, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, or
      * C, a *note complex: (Complexes)Complex,, 
      * Cplus, a *note complex: (Complexes)Complex,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Threshold (missing documentation) => a *note real number:
        (Macaulay2Doc)RR,, default value 1e-10, an absolute error up to which
        the identities should hold
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, 

Description
===========

The functions returns true, if the Penrose relations A*B*A == A, B*A*B == B,
A*B==transpose(A*B) and B*A=transpose(B*A)) are satisfied. In case of an
inexact field the relation should hold up to a threshold. In case of two chain
complexes, these relation should hold for each pair of pseudo inverse
differentials.

