File: SVDComplexes.info, Node: pseudoInverse, Next: pseudoInverse1, Prev: projectToComplex, Up: Top

pseudoInverse -- compute the pseudoInverse of a chain complex
*************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        Cplus = pseudoInverse C
  * Inputs:
      * C, a *note complex: (Complexes)Complex,, an approximate complex over an
        field
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Strategy (missing documentation) => a *note symbol:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Symbol,, default value Projection, Laplacian or
        Projection for the method used
      * Threshold (missing documentation) => a *note real number:
        (Macaulay2Doc)RR,, default value .0001, the relative threshold used to
        detect the zero singular values
  * Outputs:
      * Cplus, a *note complex: (Complexes)Complex,, the pseudo inverse complex

Description
===========

In case the field is RR we use the SVD normal form to compute the pseudo
inverse. In case of QQ we compute the pseudo inverse directly over QQ.

