SVDHomology -- Estimate the homology of a chain complex over RR with the SVD decomposition
******************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        (h,h1)=SVDHomology C or
        (h,h1)=SVDHomology(C,C')
  * Inputs:
      * C, a *note complex: (Complexes)Complex,, over RR_{53}
      * C', a *note complex: (Complexes)Complex,, in a lower precision
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Strategy => a *note symbol: (Macaulay2Doc)Symbol,, default value
        Projection, Laplacian or Projection for the method used
      * Threshold => a *note real number: (Macaulay2Doc)RR,, default value
        .0001, the relative threshold used to detect the zero singular values
  * Outputs:
      * h, a *note hash table: (Macaulay2Doc)HashTable,, the dimensions of the
        homology groups HH C
      * h1, a *note hash table: (Macaulay2Doc)HashTable,, information about the
        singular values

Description
===========

We compute the singular value decomposition either by the iterated Projections
or by the Laplacian method. In case of the projection method we record in h1
the last two nonzero singular values and first singular value expected to be
really zero.

In case of the Laplacian method we record in h1 the smallest common Eigenvalues
of the neighboring Laplacians, and the first Eigenvalue expected to be zero.

In case the input consists of two chain complexes we use the iterated
Projection method, and identify the stable singular values.

